    TensorRT 11.3.0.99: tuner 2.21.55, 215 knobs
    measured earlier on TensorRT 11.1.0.106: tuner 2.19.45, 209 knobs
    -> the builder gained 6 knobs between those two releases while the API shape did not change
============================== End   [case_tuner_version_is_a_finer_fingerprint]
============================== Start [case_set_a_route,(),{}]
    default build_route = ''
    after assignment     = '-conv_use_long_w=off'

    baseline plan size, 5 identical builds: [34860, 34476, 34860, 34860, 34860]
    -> 2 distinct value(s), spread 384 B on a 34,476 B plan
       The builder times tactics; a tie broken differently changes the plan. So a single
       build is not a baseline, and `size != baseline` is not evidence of anything.
       Band used below, with a 1,024 B margin: (33452, 35884)
============================== End   [case_set_a_route]
============================== Start [case_accepted_is_not_applied,(),{}]
    baseline band 33,452 .. 35,884 B

    route                                plan size   verdict
    -conv_use_long_w=off                    34,476   inside the baseline band - no evidence of any effect
    -conv_lowering=off                      34,476   inside the baseline band - no evidence of any effect
    -reshape_ppg=off                        34,476   inside the baseline band - no evidence of any effect
    -transpose_ppg=off                      34,860   inside the baseline band - no evidence of any effect

    Each one came back echoed by the tuner as `[TuningBuildRoute] Using build route: ...`,
    so they all reached the builder - the route is not being dropped on the floor.

    -> and yet none of them moved the plan out of the noise band. Acceptance is not
       effect: a knob acts on a pattern that has to be present, and a 64x64 MatMul
       gives most of them nothing to do. Same trap as `02-API/BuilderFlag/`.
============================== End   [case_accepted_is_not_applied]
============================== Start [case_wrong_input_is_handled_asymmetrically,(),{}]
    route                         built   echoed by tuner         message
    -no_such_knob=on              False   -                       Build route knob '-no_such_knob' is not a valid knob. Use IB
    garbage                       False   -                       Build route token 'garbage' must match format -name=value (w
    -conv_use_long_w              False   -                       Build route token '-conv_use_long_w' must match format -name
    -conv_use_long_w=maybe        True    -conv_use_long_w=maybe

    -> the name is validated, the value is not, and the one case that silently does
       nothing is also the one the tuner claims to be using. Check a route against
       `all_build_routes` yourself; TensorRT will not do it for you.
